  "query_preview": "..\nAs TD 07W continues to move W away from the Marianas, the southeast \ninflow will keep scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms \npossible for Guam throughout tonight before improving to isolated \ncoverage on Saturday. As for the CNMI, decided to keep low-end (30%)\nscattered showers but ommitted thunderstorm potential due to\nsatellite trends showing any possible convection being sheared off.\nModel guidance shows the northeastern extent of TD 07W's tail\nreinvigorating tomorrow, so the CNMI will remain at scattered shower\ncoverage throughout Saturday afternoon. High pressure will follow TD\n07W, so drier conditions are expected for the Marianas starting\nSaturday night. Winds may become light and variable starting Sunday,\nso island-effect showers and isolated thunderstorms may be possible\nin the afternoon hours for all islands through at least the first\nhalf of next week.",
